WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.130
Long hydrocarbon molecules from
crude oil are thick and hard to

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:04.910
use.

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.270
So a refinery cracks them,

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.490
snapping each long molecule
into shorter, more useful ones.

5
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.450
But the pieces are
never all the same kind.

6
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.730
One piece always has fewer
hydrogen atoms than it seems it

7
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.910
should.

8
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.410
What is that hydrogen-short molecule,

9
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.590
and why do chemical
companies want it so badly?

10
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.500
In this mission, you'll crack
long alkanes into shorter ones.

11
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.210
You'll meet alkenes
and their double bond,

12
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.010
test for them with bromine water,

13
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.050
and see how they become the
starting point for making polymers.

14
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.470
Your mission: explain what cracking
makes, and why it matters.
